                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Use the ShapeDiver Output component to define geometry outputs that can be baked back to a desktop client.

The ShapeDiver Output also doubles as a display component in the web viewer; there is no need to also include Display components. Materials can be defined through attributes before sending the geometry to the component.

You can add several geometry "chunks" in the output by zooming and clicking on the + handle.

The component's name (in our case "Floors") is the name of the output in the final App. Each "chunk" is also identified separately in the UI.</item>
                  </items>
