                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Geometry outputs for desktop clients are typed! This is important, because some geometry types are not compatible with all desktop clients. For example, it is not possible to send meshes to Adobe Illustrator.

Before sending geometry to  a ShapeDiver Output component, it needs to go through a floating parameter of the specific geometry type you want to output.

The name of the floating parameter also defines the name of this data "chunk" in the ShapeDiver Output component. In this example, we send a list of meshes called "Volumes" and a list of curves called "Edges".</item>
